this and more with senate minority  leader mitch mcconnell  senator welcome back to special report  hey brett  i want to start with the covid relief  bill  this was president biden this afternoon  about  about that bill take a listen  critics say the plan is too big that it  costs too much  but let me ask a rhetorical question  what would you have me  cut what would you have me cut out  what would you have him cut senator  that's a good question first of all the  minimum wage doesn't belong in there the  congressional budget office says it  would cost  1.4 million jobs we'd  lose second 350 billion dollars for  bailouts to poorly run states  clearly not necessary with regard to the  school funding that they  added by the way the school funding that  we've already provided is not yet spent  out  in a bill we passed just a couple of  months ago  but of the school funding that they add  only five percent of it is used this  year  the rest of it spent out in future years  i thought this was  supposed to be a package about covet  relief  this is wildly more expensive brett  than the country needs at this  particular time because the vaccines are  rolling out  shots are getting into arms the economy  is  getting better and better i think  my 10 moderate republicans went down to  see the president suggested  that they could justify about five or  six hundred  billion dollars this is two trillion to  put that in context that's what we spent  at the height  of the pandemic last april it's  wildly too expensive and full of  democratic  ass that they want to take advantage of  under the name of covet relief  so do you expect to lose any republicans  on this bill  well certainly hope not we didn't lose  any on the  first round which was the budget which  makes possible  the second round the budget  reconciliation that we expect  to get over from the house soon  do you think that democrats are  positioning uh possibly  not only with covid this covet bill but  other bills  to try to use reconciliation the process  by which they only need  50 plus one yeah they they are  and they will probably try to do one  more  and in it you can anticipate all of your  taxes going up  business taxes going up which of course  will be bad for the economy  individual taxes going up now these guys  live to raise taxes and no matter what  they call the next package  you can anticipate it'll have a very  significant tax increase for the  american people  senator back under president bush 43  you were a proponent of ear marks so  right now  should congress reinstate earmarks  restore that spending authority  essentially went to the executive branch  yeah i think earmarks are very unpopular  among republicans i think we're very  unenthusiastic there may be some  republicans  interested in that's sort of  what's called congressionally directed  spending it doesn't enjoy much  support among republicans either in the  house or the senate  so you've switched your thinking about  it obviously you were a proponent before  well i represent the entire conference  and i can tell you the overwhelming  majority of the  republican conference in the senate is  not in favorable even if the democrats  craft the bill so that those are  permitted  will not be asking for them i want to  talk about nominees  specifically nira tandon why do you want  to hold the gop  line on the omb director nominee near  attendant  well she's excessively partisan  [Music]  she tweeted frequently we're  accustomed to that these days but she  took  shots at everybody she's taken  offensive shots at almost all of my  members  you think of people in charge of omb  as being kind of honest brokers that you  can talk to and she's been  so partisan that she's generated  opposition from even my most  moderate members for example like  senator collins  senator romney who are always looking  for opportunities to be cooperative with  the administration  this is just another example of the fact  that the president has chosen  a very progressive beginning his chief  of staff on msnbc yesterday  said with regard to the covet package  the most progressive  legislation in a generation the  president has decided not to be a  centrist  and therefore he shouldn't expect much  republican support for these kind of  initiatives  you know democrats point to trump  nominees like rick grinnell who is a  prolific  partisan tweeter who did not have any  problem getting through a confirmation  vote but more importantly  critics of this hold up say  you know republicans didn't even address  some of president trump's tweets  that dealt specifically with people yeah  i think a lot of my members chose not to  comment on the president's daily  tweeting  i was among them and we concluded that  was not a constructive use of our time  so you don't think there's a difference  there as far as  holding one side accountable or not  well i think when it comes to being  confirmed  your record is before the senate the  senate's in the personnel business  unlike the house and so when members  come up for confirmation their whole  record  is before us and in this day and age  tweeting is part of your record  all right we're just 12 days senator  since you're really blistering speech on  the senate floor  about former president trump here's just  a piece of that  he did not do his job  he didn't take steps so federal law  could be  faithfully executed and order restored  no instead  according to public reports he watched  television happily  happily as the chaos unfolded  sorry i interrupted you there with your  your speech uh  you were saying well look my point is  what happened in the past is not  something relevant now we're moving  forward  we've got a new administration it's a  very left-wing administration we need to  make sure the american people understand  that this is not what republicans stand  for  i want to say this about the president  having chosen the progressive  route he certainly made it a lot easier  for me to unify  my members in opposition  you're talking about president biden but  the reason it's relevant and obviously  i'm sure you read the lengthy statement  from  the former president saying the  republican party can never again be  respected or strong with political  leaders like senator mitch mcconnell at  its helm  mcconnell's dedication to business as  usual status quo policies together with  his  lack of political insight wisdom skill  and personality has rapidly driven him  from majority leader to minority leader  it goes on very specifically when you  read that what was your reaction  the republican party is actually in very  good shape  we gained seats in the house we  elected 50 republican senators when  everybody was predicting we were going  to lose the senate  the democrats didn't flip a single state  legislature  we flipped two picked up a governor the  republican party had a very good day on  november 3rd  we're sorry we lost the white house but  the republican party  demonstrated once again this is a 50-50  nation  we're very competitive and we'll be  competitive again  in 22. do you blame the former president  for losing the two georgia  senate seats i don't have any further  observations to make  about that we're looking forward okay  dealing with the new administration  and trying to hold the senate in 22. let  me you know it's ahead of this big  speech this weekend at cpac  should the former president be speaking  at cpac this weekend  i don't have any advice to give the  former president about where he should  speak or what he should say  okay is there a civil war in the gop  currently  no i think if you're looking for a real  civil war look at the democrats in the  house  the progressives making it extremely  difficult  for speaker pelosi to operate give them  a narrow  margin she has overall in the house  i think the biden administration is  making it easy for us to get together  and  i think we've unified in opposition to  this new administration's extremely  progressive  approach president biden has made it  quite easy for us to get together  the there'll be a lot of talk this  weekend about 2024 and whether the  former president is going to get in that  mix here's what senator romney  said about that if he does  will president trump continue to play a  role in my party i'm sure he will  he has by far the largest voice and a  big impact in my party  i don't know about his family members  whether they intend to do that  but but i expect he will continue  playing a role i don't know if he'll run  in 2024 or not but if he does  i yeah i'm pretty sure he will win the  nomination  you agree with that well there's a lot  to happen between now and 24 i've got at  least four members that i think are  planning on running for president plus  some for  some governors and others there's no  incumbent  should be a wide open race and fun for  you all to cover  if the president was the party's nominee  would you support him  uh the nominee of the party absolutely  i want to ask you a couple more things  the 911 style commission that speaker  pelosi is talking about for january 6th  obviously what you said on the floor was  very specific you voted to acquit  but there's an investigation into what  happened that day on all elements of  security  are you for or against that  far against investigating well some of  our committees have been having hearings  on that very subject  this week i'm open to a 9 11  type commission but it's got to be even  like the 9 11 commission was if we're  going to  do an outside commission review of the  events of january 6. it needs to be  structured  similar to the 911 commission and you  might have noticed that the chairs of  the 911 commission have already  come out against nancy pelosi's approach  to this because it's not balanced  that one was balanced both lee hamilton  and tom kane who chaired that outside  commission  back after 9 11 even refused to go on  sunday shows  except together it was a totally  bipartisan effort that's what's needed  in order to have  credibility attached to the final report  that kind of commission i'm open to  nothing  close to what the speaker's uh proposing  i'm  open to senator i only have 30 seconds  left but what would you say the trump  supporters  who read the president's statement about  you  and are concerned about the future of  the gop  what i would say to everybody who's  inclined to support  our right of center republican party  let's focus on winning  the house and the senate in 22  that will set up the next nominee for  president whoever that may be  the best chance to be victorious  senator i always have more questions for  you wish i had more time but we  appreciate your time on special report  thanks a lot

